{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "PRO",
  "chapter": 5,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PRO.5.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.5.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My son, attend to my wisdom, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " bow thy ear to my understanding:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.5.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.5.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That thou mayest regard discretion, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thy lips may keep knowledge.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.5.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.5.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the lips of a strange woman drop ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a honey-comb, and her mouth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " smoother than oil:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.5.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.5.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But her end is bitter as wormwood, sharp as a two-edged sword.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.5.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.5.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Her feet go down to death; her steps take hold on hell.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.5.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.5.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Lest thou shouldst ponder the path of life, her ways are movable, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thou canst not know ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.5.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.5.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hear me now therefore, O ye children, and depart not from the words of my mouth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.5.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.5.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Remove thy way far from her, and come not nigh the door of her house:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.5.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.5.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Lest thou give thy honor to others, and thy years to the cruel:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.5.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.5.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Lest strangers be filled with thy wealth; and thy labors ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in the house of a stranger;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.5.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.5.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And thou mourn at the last, when thy flesh and thy body are consumed,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.5.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.5.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And say, How have I hated instruction, and my heart despised reproof;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.5.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.5.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And have not obeyed the voice of my teachers, nor inclined my ear to them that instructed me!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.5.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.5.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I was almost in all evil in the midst of the congregation and assembly.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.5.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.5.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Drink waters out of thy own cistern, and running waters out of thy own well.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.5.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.5.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let thy fountains be dispersed abroad, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " rivers of waters in the streets.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.5.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.5.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let them be only thy own, and not for strangers with thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.5.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.5.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let thy fountain be blessed: and rejoice with the wife of thy youth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.5.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.5.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let her be as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the loving hind and pleasant roe; let her breasts satisfy thee at all times; and be thou ravished always with her love.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.5.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.5.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And why wilt thou, my son, be ravished with a strange woman, and embrace the bosom of a stranger?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.5.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.5.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the ways of man ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " before the eyes of the LORD, and he pondereth all his goings.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.5.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.5.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "His own iniquities shall take the wicked himself, and he shall be held with the cords of his sins.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.5.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.5.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He shall die without instruction; and in the greatness of his folly he shall go astray.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
